at="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEDA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKI, SHOGO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, RYOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDE, TAKUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKAYA KOHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEDA HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIKI SHOGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO RYOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIDE TAKUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKAYA, KOHEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEDA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKI, SHOGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, RYOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDE, TAKUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A balloon catheter used in therapy or operation for the purpose of expanding a lesion region mainly such as constriction part and occlusion part in an endogenous passage. In the conventional expansion catheter, a fixing portion "tip" of a tubular member for passing an expansion body and a guide wire therethrough is hard, so that there has been a problem in operability due to insufficient following properties on the curvy endogenous passage and insufficient guide wire sliding properties due to a difference in flexibility from the guide wire used in combination. The balloon catheter is a catheter characterized in that it has a structure, in which a tubular member for passing a guide wire therethrough is disposed through an inside of an expansion body, and the expansion body and an outer face of the tubular body are concentrically welded in the vicinity of a distal end of the catheter, and that a Shore hardness of a material constituting an outermost face of the tubular member is lower than that of a material constituting the expansion body, so that it is possible to flexibly adjust a tip portion formed by fixing the expansion body and the tubular member for passing a guide wire therethrough.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un cathéter à ballonnet utilisé à des fins thérapeutiques ou chirurgicales pour élargir une zone de lésion (constriction ou occlusion par exemple) dans un passage endogène. Dans le cas d'un cathéter à expansion classique, l'extrémité de fixation de l'élément tubulaire par laquelle passent le dispositif d'expansion et le fil de guidage est dure, ce qui pose un problème d'utilisation par suite des difficultés d'insertion dans les parties courbes du passage endogène et de la capacité de glissement insuffisante du fil de guidage à cause de différences de flexibilité. La cathéter à ballonnet se caractérise en ce qu'il comporte une structure dont l'élément tubulaire pour le passage du fil de guidage est disposé à l'intérieur d'un corps d'expansion, ce corps d'expansion et le bord extérieur de l'élément tubulaire étant soudés l'un à l'autre à leur périphérie à proximité de l'extrémité distale du cathéter. Par ailleurs, le degré de dureté Shore du matériau utilisé pour le bord externe de l'élément tubulaire est inférieur au degré de dureté Shore du matériau constituant le corps d'expansion. On dispose ainsi d'une souplesse suffisante pour régler la partie extrémité formée par La fixation du corps d'expansion et de l'élément tubulaire où passe le fil de guidage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>